Getting started
---------------

Initialize the RealizeUI:

```
repo init -u https://github.com/RealizeUI/android.git -b 16 --git-lfs --depth 1
```


Sync up
---------------

```
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

Build
---------------
•Set up the build environment:
```
. b*/env*
```

•Select target:
```
lunch lineage_$codename-bp4a-user
```
•To start compiling
```
m bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

Feature source policy
---------------

RealizeUI uses the Lunaris 16.2 framework stack as its initial feature donor.
That stack already integrates the Axion SDK and is declared separately in
`snippets/realizeui-features.xml` so it can be replaced incrementally with
RealizeUI forks.

The donor Settings applications and customization frontends are intentionally
excluded. `packages/apps/Settings` is maintained by RealizeUI on branch `16`,
and all RealizeUI feature preferences must be implemented there. RealizeUI also
keeps its own `vendor/lineage`; packages from the feature snippet must be added
to RealizeUI product configuration explicitly before they are included in an
image.
